Who is the greatest?
At that time, the disciples came to Jesus and asked him, "Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?"
Then Jesus called a little child to him, and set him in the midst of them:
He said: "I tell you the truth, unless you change and become like little children, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven."
Therefore whoever humbles himself like this child is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.
"And whoever kisses this child in my name is kissing me." Warning against stumbling blocks
But if anyone causes one of these little ones who believe in me to sin—it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be drowned in the sea.
Woe to the world for these stumbling blocks that must come, but woe to those who cause them!
Therefore if your hand or foot causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away; it is better for you to enter life maimed than with two hands or two feet to be thrown into eternal fire.
If your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out and throw it away from you. It is better for you to enter life with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hellfire." The Lost Sheep
Jesus said: "Beware that you do not despise one of these little ones; for I say to you that their angels in heaven always see the face of my Father who is in heaven."
For the Son of Man came to seek and save what was lost.
What do you think about a man who has 100 sheep and loses one? Won't he leave the 99 in the mountains to go find the lost sheep?
I tell you the truth, when he finds it, he will be more joyful over that one sheep than over the ninety-nine who didn't get lost.
That's also why your Father in heaven doesn't want one of these simple disciples to perish. Be reconciled with your brother.
If your brother wrongs you, go to him in private and talk with him. If he listens to you, then you have won over your brother.
But if he won't listen to you, take one or two others along with you, so that every matter may be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses. #Two or three witnesses. 16:18 See Deuteronomy 19:15.
If he refuses to listen to them, tell it to the church. If he refuses to listen to the church, then you must treat him like an idolater or tax collector.
I tell you the truth, whatever you bind on earth will be bound in heaven, and whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.
I tell you the truth, if two of you agree about anything you ask for, it will be done for you by my Father in heaven.
"For where two or three gather in my name, there am I with them." Forgiveness without limits
Then Peter came to Jesus and asked, "Lord, how many times shall I forgive my brother or sister who sins against me? Up to seven times?"
فقال له يسوع: "مش بس سبع مرات، لكن سبعين مرة في المرة الواحدة!" #سبعين... مرات. 22:18 يعني من غير حد.
Therefore, the kingdom of heaven can be compared to a king who decided to settle accounts with his servants.
When he started settling his accounts, a man who owed him an enormous sum came to him. #An enormous amount. 24:18 Literally: "Ten thousand talents or minas, which is equivalent to about 300,000 kilograms of coins used at that time."
Since he couldn't pay off his debt, Mr. decided to sell the debtor along with his wife and children and all his possessions, using the money to settle the debt.
Then the slave fell down at his master's feet and begged him to give him time, saying he would pay off all that was due.
The gentleman felt sorry for him, cancelled his debt completely, and let him go.
As he was walking along, one of his fellow slaves, who owed him some money, grabbed hold of him by the neck to make him pay up.
The servant prostrated himself before him, begging for mercy, saying: "Give me time to pay what I owe."
But he refused to do so; instead, he took him off to prison until he paid all his debts.
When other slaves saw what happened they were really sad and went to tell their master everything that had occurred.
His master called him in and said to him, "You wicked servant! I forgave you your entire debt because you begged me to."
Why didn't you show mercy to your servant friend just like I showed mercy to you?
His master was furious and handed him over to be punished until he paid off his debts.
"That is how your heavenly Father will also treat you if each one of you does not forgive his brother from your heart."
Union in marriage
After Jesus finished speaking about these things, he left Galilee and went to Judea across the Jordan River.
And large crowds followed him there and he healed them.
Some Pharisees came to Jesus testing him, saying, "Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any cause?"
Jesus replied, "Haven't you read in the book of Genesis that from the beginning God created them male and female?" #male...and female. 4:19 From Genesis 1:27, 5:2
Then he said: "For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and they will become one flesh." #leaves...one. Genesis 2:24
And so they will never be two again but one. Therefore, let no man separate what God has joined together."
They said to him: "Why then did Moses command that when a man gives his wife a certificate of divorce, #certificate of divorce. 7:19 See Deuteronomy 24:1. should she be set free?"
Jesus replied, "Moses permitted you to divorce your wives because your hearts were hard. But it was not this way from the beginning."
"That's why I tell you that anyone who divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, commits adultery if he marries another woman."
His disciples said to him: "If this is how it is between husband and wife, then it's better not to get married!"
Jesus said to them, "Not everyone can accept this teaching, but only those whom God has given the ability to do so."
